<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>AI Summer Camp - Congratulations!</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/final.css">
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.4.0/css/all.min.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="lobby-card">
            <div class="header-section">
                <a href="/logout" class="logout-btn">
                    <i class="fas fa-sign-out-alt"></i>
                    Logout
                </a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="user-section">
                <div class="celebration-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-trophy"></i>
                </div>
                <h1 class="congratulations-title">Congratulations, <%= user.name %>!</h1>
                <div class="achievement-text">
                    <p>You've successfully completed the INTRODUCTION! (Yes, this is just the introduction!)</p>
                </div>
                <div class="score-section">
                    <div class="final-score-display">
                        <span class="score-label">Final Score:</span>
                        <span class="score-value"><%= user.score || 0 %> points</span>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="ai-description">
                <h2 class="description-title">The Foundation of AI: Programming</h2>
                <p class="description-text">
                    All these remarkable AI advances, from recognizing patterns to understanding human language, are only 
                    made possible because machines can <strong>mimic human intelligence</strong>. But how do we bridge 
                    the gap between human thinking and machine processing?
                </p>
                <p class="description-text">
                    The first step in mimicking human intelligence is learning <strong>communication</strong>. Just as 
                    humans use language to express thoughts and ideas, we need a way to communicate our logic to machines.
                </p>
                <p class="description-text highlight-section">
                    This is where <strong>programming</strong> becomes crucial. Programming is the language that helps us 
                    adapt our human logic into <span class="highlight">machine-ready instructions</span>. It's the 
                    bridge that transforms our creative problem-solving abilities into code that computers can execute.
                </p>
                <p class="description-text">
                    Every AI system you've learned about—classification, regression, natural language processing—begins 
                    with programmers writing code that teaches machines to think and learn. Programming isn't just about 
                    writing instructions; it's about <strong>translating human intelligence into digital form</strong>.
                </p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="journey-complete">
                <div class="journey-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="journey-title">Let's start coding!</h3>
                <p class="journey-text">
                    You've explored the fascinating world of Artificial Intelligence and discovered the power of programming 
                    as the foundation that makes it all possible. Let's embark on the next step of your journey
                    together and dive into the world of coding!
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="/js/final.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
